		<!--Credits (e.g., model author names) associated with the model.-->
		<credits>A 2-D model 11 degrees of freedom and 18 muscles for simulating walking. This model was assembled by Vinh Nguyen and Russel Johnson and includes elements from Delp et al. (1990), Yamaguchi Zajac (1989), Anderson Pandy (1999), Sasaki et al. (2009) and Porsa et al. (2016). The CustomJoint and moving muscle insertion points for the knee joint are due to Ajay Seth. For use with Moco, Brian Umberger replaced the muscles with DeGrooteFregly2016Muscles and the ground contact elements with SmoothSphereHalfSpaceForces. License: Creative Commons (CCBY 3.0). You are free to distribute, remix, tweak, and build upon this work, even commercially, as long as you credit us for the original creation.</credits>
		<!--Publications and references associated with the model.-->
		<publications>&gt;Nguyen, V.Q.,Johnson, R.T., Sup, F.C., Umberger, B.R. Bilevel Optimization for Cost Function Determination in Dynamic Simulation of Human Gait. IEEE Transactions on Neural Systems and Rehabilitation Engineering, vol 27 pp 1426-1435, 2019</publications>
		<!--Units for all lengths.-->
		<length_units>meters</length_units>
		<!--Units for all forces.-->
		<force_units>N</force_units>
